#: ../../architecture.rst:92
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The transmitter embeds a binary message into the chaotic carrier via "
"Pecora-Carroll modulation: :math:`s[n] = x_1[n] + \\mu \\cdot m[n]`. The "
"channel applies distortion (ideal pass-through, FIR band-limiting, AWGN, "
"multipath, or composite urban model). The receiver synchronises to the "
"carrier and recovers the message estimate :math:`\\hat{m}[n] \\approx "
"m[n]`."
msgstr "The transmitter embeds a binary message into the chaotic carrier via Pecora-Carroll modulation: :math:`s[n] = x_1[n] + \\\\mu \\\\cdot m[n]`. The channel applies distortion (ideal pass-through, FIR band-limiting, AWGN, multipath, or composite urban model). The receiver synchronises to the carrier and recovers the message estimate :math:`\\\\hat{m}[n] \\\\approx m[n]`."

#: ../../architecture.rst:100
msgid "Parameter sweep pipeline"
msgstr "Pipeline de varredura de parâmetros"

#: ../../architecture.rst:102
msgid ""
"The sweep framework is the computational core of the project. Its design "
"balances raw throughput, deterministic reproducibility, and optional "
"Numba dependency:"
msgstr ""
"O framework de varredura é o núcleo computacional do projeto. Seu design "
"equilibra vazão bruta, reprodutibilidade determinística e dependência "
"opcional de Numba:"

#: ../../architecture.rst:125
msgid ""
"Every hot loop is Numba-JIT compiled. The outer loop is a single "
"``prange`` where tasks are **interleaved** (not chunked) via the permuted"
" task order, balancing thread load across the heterogeneous (high-cutoff "
"= many-tap = slow, low-cutoff = few-tap = fast) grid points."
msgstr ""
"Todo laço crítico é compilado via Numba-JIT. O laço externo é um único "
"``prange`` onde as tarefas são **intercaladas** (não particionadas em "
"blocos) via ordem de tarefas permutada, balanceando a carga entre threads"
" ao longo dos pontos heterogêneos da grade (corte alto = muitos taps = "
"lento, corte baixo = poucos taps = rápido)."

#: ../../architecture.rst:132
msgid "Key design decisions"
msgstr "Decisões de Design"

#: ../../architecture.rst:134
msgid ""
"**Numba as an optional accelerator.** The package imports and runs "
"correctly without Numba installed. All JIT-compiled kernels fall back to "
"pure Python via :mod:`chaotic_pfc._compat`: a thin compatibility layer "
"that no-ops ``njit``, aliases ``prange`` to ``range``, and returns ``1`` "
"for ``get_num_threads()``. Install the ``[fast]`` extra for 20–50× "
"speedup on the sweep."
msgstr "**Numba como acelerador opcional.** O pacote importa e executa corretamente sem o Numba instalado. Todos os kernels compilados em JIT recaem para Python puro via :mod:`chaotic_pfc._compat`: uma fina camada de compatibilidade que transforma ``njit`` em no-op, mapeia ``prange`` para ``range`` e retorna ``1`` para ``get_num_threads()``. Instale o extra ``[fast]`` para ganho de 20–50× na varredura."

#: ../../architecture.rst:141
msgid ""
"**Deterministic reproducibility.** Perturbation vectors are pre-generated"
" on the Python side using ``default_rng(seed)`` and passed as NumPy "
"arrays into the Numba kernel. This is necessary because Numba's per-"
"thread RNG does not honour the global seed. Every run with the same seed "
"produces bit-exact identical results."
msgstr "**Reprodutibilidade determinística.** Os vetores de perturbação são pré-gerados no lado Python usando ``default_rng(seed)`` e passados como arrays NumPy para o kernel Numba. Isso é necessário porque o RNG por thread do Numba não respeita a semente global. Cada execução com a mesma semente produz resultados idênticos byte a byte."

#: ../../architecture.rst:147
msgid ""
"**Lazy optional imports.** 3-D visualisation requires ``plotly`` "
"installed via the ``[viz3d]`` extra. The import is deferred until "
":mod:`chaotic_pfc.analysis.sweep_plotting_3d` is actually used, so "
"``import chaotic_pfc`` always succeeds. The same pattern applies to "
":samp:`scipy.signal.firwin` imports within dataclass methods."
msgstr "**Importações opcionais sob demanda.** A visualização 3‑D requer ``plotly`` instalado via o extra ``[viz3d]``. A importação é adiada até que :mod:`chaotic_pfc.analysis.sweep_plotting_3d` seja efetivamente usado, de modo que ``import chaotic_pfc`` sempre funciona. O mesmo padrão se aplica a importações de :samp:`scipy.signal.firwin` dentro de métodos de dataclasses."

#: ../../architecture.rst:153
msgid ""
"**Structural protocols.** :mod:`chaotic_pfc.comms.protocols` defines "
"``typing.Protocol`` classes: ``Transmitter``, ``Channel``, ``Receiver``: "
"as structural contracts. Concrete implementations (``transmit``, "
"``ideal_channel``, ``receive``, etc.) satisfy these protocols by duck "
"typing. This provides mypy-level documentation of the communication "
"pipeline's interface without runtime overhead."
msgstr "**Protocolos estruturais.** :mod:`chaotic_pfc.comms.protocols` define classes ``typing.Protocol``: ``Transmitter``, ``Channel``, ``Receiver``: como contratos estruturais. Implementações concretas (``transmit``, ``ideal_channel``, ``receive``, etc.) satisfazem esses protocolos por duck typing. Isso fornece documentação em nível mypy da interface do pipeline de comunicação sem sobrecarga em tempo de execução."

#: ../../architecture.rst:160
msgid ""
"**Shallow config hierarchy.** All defaults reside in "
":mod:`chaotic_pfc.config` as dataclasses. The hierarchy is intentionally "
"shallow: every sub-config has only primitive fields or nested dataclasses"
" of primitives: enabling trivial copying (``dataclasses.replace``), test "
"isolation, and serialisation (``dataclasses.asdict``)."
msgstr "**Hierarquia de configuração rasa.** Todos os padrões residem em :mod:`chaotic_pfc.config` como dataclasses. A hierarquia é intencionalmente rasa: cada sub-config possui apenas campos primitivos ou dataclasses aninhadas de primitivos: permitindo cópia trivial (``dataclasses.replace``), isolamento de testes e serialização (``dataclasses.asdict``)."

#: ../../architecture.rst:167
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Single ``prange`` with load balancing.** The sweep kernel uses a single"
" parallel region (not nested parallelism) with a permuted task order. "
"Tasks with different filter orders have vastly different per-iteration "
"costs (the MGS inner loop scales as :math:`\\mathcal{O}(N_s^3)`), so "
"simple block partitioning would leave threads idle. Interleaving ensures "
"that each thread sees a balanced mix of light and heavy tasks."
msgstr "**Single ``prange`` with load balancing.** The sweep kernel uses a single parallel region (not nested parallelism) with a permuted task order. Tasks with different filter orders have vastly different per-iteration costs (the MGS inner loop scales as :math:`\\\\mathcal{O}(N_s^3)`), so simple block partitioning would leave threads idle. Interleaving ensures that each thread sees a balanced mix of light and heavy tasks."

#: ../../architecture.rst:175
#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"**Adaptive early-stop.** The Lyapunov estimator implements an optional "
"early-stop criterion: if :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` stabilises within a "
"specified tolerance for a streak of consecutive checkpoints, the "
"remaining iterations are skipped. This provides 3–4× speedup over fixed-"
"iteration computation with negligible accuracy loss (< 0.1% in "
":math:`\\lambda_{\\max}`)."
msgstr "**Adaptive early-stop.** The Lyapunov estimator implements an optional early-stop criterion: if :math:`\\\\lambda_{\\\\max}` stabilises within a specified tolerance for a streak of consecutive checkpoints, the remaining iterations are skipped. This provides 3–4× speedup over fixed-iteration computation with negligible accuracy loss (< 0.1% in :math:`\\\\lambda_{\\\\max}`)."

